---@field registryId? aws.ecr_public.RegistryId The Amazon Web Services account ID that's associated with the public registry that contains the repository.
---@field repositoryName? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName The name of the repository.
---@field repositoryUri? aws.ecr_public.Url The URI for the repository. You can use this URI for container image push and pull operations.
---@field createdAt? aws.ecr_public.CreationTimestamp The date and time, in JavaScript date format, when the repository was created.

---The catalog data for a repository. This data is publicly visible in the Amazon ECR Public Gallery.
---@class aws.ecr_public.RepositoryCatalogData
---@field description? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryDescription The short description of the repository.
---@field architectures? aws.ecr_public.ArchitectureList The architecture tags that are associated with the repository.
---@field operatingSystems? aws.ecr_public.OperatingSystemList The operating system tags that are associated with the repository.
---@field logoUrl? aws.ecr_public.ResourceUrl The URL that contains the logo that's associated with the repository.
---@field aboutText? aws.ecr_public.AboutText The longform description of the contents of the repository. This text appears in the repository details on the Amazon ECR Public Gallery.
---@field usageText? aws.ecr_public.UsageText The longform usage details of the contents of the repository. The usage text provides context for users of the repository.
---@field marketplaceCertified? aws.ecr_public.MarketplaceCertified Indicates whether the repository is certified by Amazon Web Services Marketplace.

---An object that contains the catalog data for a repository. This data is publicly visible in the Amazon ECR Public Gallery.
---@class aws.ecr_public.RepositoryCatalogDataInput
---@field description? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryDescription A short description of the contents of the repository. This text appears in both the image details and also when searching for repositories on the Amazon ECR Public Gallery.
---@field architectures? aws.ecr_public.ArchitectureList The system architecture that the images in the repository are compatible with. On the Amazon ECR Public Gallery, the following supported architectures appear as badges on the repository and are used as search filters.
---@field operatingSystems? aws.ecr_public.OperatingSystemList The operating systems that the images in the repository are compatible with. On the Amazon ECR Public Gallery, the following supported operating systems appear as badges on the repository and are used as search filters.
---@field logoImageBlob? aws.ecr_public.LogoImageBlob The base64-encoded repository logo payload.
---@field aboutText? aws.ecr_public.AboutText A detailed description of the contents of the repository. It's publicly visible in the Amazon ECR Public Gallery. The text must be in markdown format.
---@field usageText? aws.ecr_public.UsageText Detailed information about how to use the contents of the repository. It's publicly visible in the Amazon ECR Public Gallery. The usage text provides context, support information, and additional usage details for users of the repository. The text must be in markdown format.

---@alias aws.ecr_public.RepositoryDescription string

---@alias aws.ecr_public.RepositoryList aws.ecr_public.Repository[]

---@alias aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName string

---@alias aws.ecr_public.RepositoryNameList aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName[]

---@alias aws.ecr_public.RepositoryPolicyText string

---@alias aws.ecr_public.ResourceUrl string

---@class aws.ecr_public.SetRepositoryPolicyRequest
---@field registryId? aws.ecr_public.RegistryId The Amazon Web Services account ID that's associated with the registry that contains the repository. If you do not specify a registry, the default public registry is assumed.
---@field repositoryName aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName The name of the repository to receive the policy.
---@field policyText aws.ecr_public.RepositoryPolicyText The JSON repository policy text to apply to the repository. For more information, see Amazon ECR Repository Policies in the Amazon Elastic Container Registry User Guide.
---@field force? aws.ecr_public.ForceFlag If the policy that you want to set on a repository policy would prevent you from setting another policy in the future, you must force the SetRepositoryPolicy operation. This prevents accidental repository lockouts.

---@class aws.ecr_public.SetRepositoryPolicyResponse
---@field registryId? aws.ecr_public.RegistryId The registry ID that's associated with the request.
---@field repositoryName? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName The repository name that's associated with the request.
---@field policyText? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryPolicyText The JSON repository policy text that's applied to the repository.

---The metadata that you apply to a resource to help you categorize and organize them. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value. You define both. Tag keys can have a maximum character length of 128 characters, and tag values can have a maximum length of 256 characters.
---@class aws.ecr_public.Tag
---@field Key? aws.ecr_public.TagKey One part of a key-value pair that make up a tag. A key is a general label that acts like a category for more specific tag values.
---@field Value? aws.ecr_public.TagValue The optional part of a key-value pair that make up a tag. A value acts as a descriptor within a tag category (key).

---@alias aws.ecr_public.TagKey string

---@alias aws.ecr_public.TagKeyList aws.ecr_public.TagKey[]

---@alias aws.ecr_public.TagList aws.ecr_public.Tag[]

---@class aws.ecr_public.TagResourceRequest
---@field resourceArn aws.ecr_public.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the resource to add tags to. Currently, the supported resource is an Amazon ECR Public repository.
---@field tags aws.ecr_public.TagList The tags to add to the resource. A tag is an array of key-value pairs. Tag keys can have a maximum character length of 128 characters, and tag values can have a maximum length of 256 characters.

---@class aws.ecr_public.TagResourceResponse

---@alias aws.ecr_public.TagValue string

---@class aws.ecr_public.UntagResourceRequest
---@field resourceArn aws.ecr_public.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the resource to delete tags from. Currently, the supported resource is an Amazon ECR Public repository.
---@field tagKeys aws.ecr_public.TagKeyList The keys of the tags to be removed.

---@class aws.ecr_public.UntagResourceResponse

---@alias aws.ecr_public.UploadId string

---@class aws.ecr_public.UploadLayerPartRequest
---@field registryId? aws.ecr_public.RegistryIdOrAlias The Amazon Web Services account ID, or registry alias, that's associated with the registry that you're uploading layer parts to. If you do not specify a registry, the default public registry is assumed.
---@field repositoryName aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName The name of the repository that you're uploading layer parts to.
---@field uploadId aws.ecr_public.UploadId The upload ID from a previous InitiateLayerUpload operation to associate with the layer part upload.
---@field partFirstByte aws.ecr_public.PartSize The position of the first byte of the layer part witin the overall image layer.
---@field partLastByte aws.ecr_public.PartSize The position of the last byte of the layer part within the overall image layer.
---@field layerPartBlob aws.ecr_public.LayerPartBlob The base64-encoded layer part payload.

---@class aws.ecr_public.UploadLayerPartResponse
---@field registryId? aws.ecr_public.RegistryId The registry ID that's associated with the request.
---@field repositoryName? aws.ecr_public.RepositoryName The repository name that's associated with the request.
---@field uploadId? aws.ecr_public.UploadId The upload ID that's associated with the request.
---@field lastByteReceived? aws.ecr_public.PartSize The integer value of the last byte that's received in the request.

